Z||000002||Songman||01-16-2001||11:23 AM||||You know, I love this board... and I love my little cars, but the popularity of this board is overwhelming! <P>I have a UBB dedicated to Merle Haggard. Merle has been a country music legend for 35+ years and we have 43 members! The Fiero was built for 5 years about 15 years ago and this board has over 1800! That is outstanding! Great job, Cliff!<P>Who would have ever thought that the Pontiac Fiero would ever be more popular than Merle Haggard?!? hehe<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||frontal lobe||01-16-2001||12:54 PM||||Well, no offense, Songman, but the Fiero always was better looking than Merle, has aged better, and arguably sounds better.  Plus, the Fiero has cross-over appeal.||||reg||1
Z||000004||88formula||01-16-2001||08:05 PM||||Some how I missed that thread that Cliff posted about the Forums history. I wonder how I did that?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Songman||01-17-2001||09:21 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by frontal lobe:<BR><B>Well, no offense, Songman, but the Fiero always was better looking than Merle, has aged better, and arguably sounds better.  Plus, the Fiero has cross-over appeal.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No offense taken... and I can agree that the Fiero looks better than Merle! heheh<P>Sounds better? Not a chance...<P>Aged better? Definitely....<P>Cross-over appeal? Apparently you haven't followed Merle's career and that is ok.  Merle has had quite a few number one hits on the pop charts over the years. Also won a couple of Grammys. And I don't even need to mention that he has won more CMA awards than anyone. Been nominated for more than anyone too. He has played the White House for three Presidents and hopes for a fourth! hehe<P>Don't let the Garth Brooks/Shania Twain 'reign of terror' fool you. These two have done nothing that Merle didn't do 30 years ago. The difference now is instant worldwide gratification and mass media. And Merle did it back in the old days when you actually had to have talent instead of just buying a deal.<P>As much as I love my little car, I seriously doubt that it will ever end up in a Hall of Fame (Merle is actually in at least two - Country Music Hall of Fame and Songwriter's Hall of Fame).... Or set records that will stand 30 years later.... Or even be called a Legend.... Chalk one up for ole Merle! heheh<P>Sorry to sound like a TV ad for Merle Haggard but the man did practically raise me so I have to give him a boost when I can... If you haven't listened to him, come on over... we'd love to enlighten you... <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/icons/icon12.gif" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/icons/icon12.gif</A> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A><p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 01-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Oreif||01-17-2001||10:21 AM||||     <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Songman:<BR><B>  As much as I love my little car, I seriously doubt that it will ever end up in a Hall of Fame (Merle is actually in at least two - Country Music Hall of Fame and Songwriter's Hall of Fame).... Or set records that will stand 30 years later.... Or even be called a Legend.... Chalk one up for ole Merle! heheh<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sorry to burst your bubble but the Fiero is in <B> 3 </B> Museums! The Museum of science and industry (Chicago), The Pontiac-Oakland Club Museum, and The Indy Pace Car Museum.<BR>I thought at one time one was in the Smithsonian but am not sure if it is fact or rumor. As for records standing time. The Fiero hasn't been around for 30 years yet. But the 1984 has the record for the only mid-engine pace car to run around the Indy track.(1984, 17 years and counting).  U.S. Congressman Bob Carr Announced on 13 September 1983 in Washington D.C., That September 13th is "Fiero Day". (When is Merle Day?) The Fiero has over 16 Awards from automotive and industrial design/engineering sources. (Merle has how many Grammy's?)<P>I'm not saying Merle is better than Fiero's, Just you should look at all the facts when comparing the both of them. Each one is famous (or Infamous   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ) for their respective places in history for what/who they are.      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">     <P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 01-17-2001).]||||reg||1
