Z||000010||frontal lobe||01-17-2001||08:20 PM||||FLAME WAR STARTED OVER MERLE VS. FIERO!!!!!<P>Just kidding.  Glad you took it that way.  Hey, we didn't know you had a personal relationship with him.  That's great.<P>Garth Brooks.  Oh, brother.  I named my English Springer Spaniel "Garth", but NOT after him.<P>I agree with you.  Kind of amazing how someone can land in a certain website of all the big world out there.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Songman||01-18-2001||01:33 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B>     Sorry to burst your bubble but the Fiero is in [b] 3 </B> Museums! The Museum of science and industry (Chicago), The Pontiac-Oakland Club Museum, and The Indy Pace Car Museum.<BR>I thought at one time one was in the Smithsonian but am not sure if it is fact or rumor. As for records standing time. The Fiero hasn't been around for 30 years yet. But the 1984 has the record for the only mid-engine pace car to run around the Indy track.(1984, 17 years and counting).  U.S. Congressman Bob Carr Announced on 13 September 1983 in Washington D.C., That September 13th is "Fiero Day". (When is Merle Day?) The Fiero has over 16 Awards from automotive and industrial design/engineering sources. (Merle has how many Grammy's?)<P>I'm not saying Merle is better than Fiero's, Just you should look at all the facts when comparing the both of them. Each one is famous (or Infamous    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ) for their respective places in history for what/who they are.       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hmmm.... Guess I better save my bubble...<BR>The list goes on.... hehehe<P>Merle's music was taken to the moon on Apollo 16.. requested by the astronauts...<P>As far as Grammy's - Merle only has two. That was mentioned in relation to crossover. In his own field he has 43 CMA awards (more than anyone) and 18 ACM awards. On the 1970 CMA show he was nominated for 9 of the 11 categories. He took 4 home! That is most nominations in one night, and most wins!<P>More - 47 country awards, 9 pop awards, 56 BMI awards, 41 #1 country singles, Today I Started Loving You Again has been recorded by over 400 other artists! Okie From Muscogee stayed at #1 on the country charts for 37 weeks!<P>And let's not confuse a museum with a Hall of Fame. He is in several Hall of Fames. Merle is in the Smithsonian as well as other museums. Not to mention receiving several 'Living Legend' awards.<P>Fender Guitars copied a custom built Telecaster-style guitar that Merle had built years earlier and released it as the 'Merle Haggard Signature Tuff-Dog Tele'.<P>Oh, and since you asked... Merle Haggard Day is... hang on, I'm looking it up. It was announced a few years ago at a special Merle Haggard Tribute at the Ryman Auditorium...<P>And did I mention playing at the White House for three presidents? And being given a Presidential Pardon by a fourth for his misspent youth.....<P>Well, you said get my facts straight... Guess I have them... heheh. I can look up more if you are interested. These are just the ones I could think of right off...<P>I love Merle and my Fieros.. and yes, I do have personal reasons for both.... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/icons/icon12.gif"> <BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000012||My7Fieros||01-18-2001||01:47 AM||||Lol...OMG! I remember when I was like 8 or 9 my step dad listening to Merle Haggard ALL the time! <B><I>EEEKKK!!!!</B></I> lol..If I hear "Roly Poly, daddy's little fatty, eatin' corn and taters all the day" one more time, Im gonna scream!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||7
Z||000013||Songman||01-18-2001||01:51 AM||||You think it was bad by Merle.. go listen to it by the Dixie Tramps!...er, I mean Dixie Chicks... heheh<P>If your stepdad is still around, tell him we'll be in Robbinsonville at Sam's Town in just a few weeks (Feb 9-10 I think)... I'm gonna try to come to Memphis and meet some Fiero friends while I am over that way.... If you are gonna be around, I would love to be able to say hello.... won't even make you go to the show and listen to Merle! hehe<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A><p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 01-18-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000014||DJRice||01-18-2001||09:44 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Songman:<BR><B>  Don't let the Garth Brooks/Shania Twain 'reign of terror' fool you. These two have done nothing that Merle didn't do 30 years ago. The difference now is instant worldwide gratification and mass media. And Merle did it back in the old days when you actually had to have talent instead of just buying a deal.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I cant see calling anything that Shania Twain does a "reign of terror".  Im not a big fan of her music, but she is very easy on the eyes.<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"You mean like the back seat of a Volkswagen?"||||reg||1
Z||000015||Songman||01-18-2001||11:04 AM||||True! She is a very beautiful woman! I met her once very briefly.. she was much smaller than I thought she would be..<P>I just meant the effect they had on 'country' music... both of them had great careers for their pocketbooks... but not good for the country music industry as a whole. Doing pop and calling it country can't be a good thing for very long.<P>Garth is trying to get back to country. He is recording an album of country standards. He recorded Merle's song, Swingin Doors, on Christmas day...<P>Wonder if either of them ever drove a Fiero? heheh<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
